02110638","approve":true,"bead_id":"bob-cli-3j.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-3j[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Excellent shell completion for bob, plus just install[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Pressing TAB after `bob` in zsh (and bash) offers grouped, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]described, vault-aware completions computed live by the installed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bob binary, so completion can never drift from the CLI; `bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]completion` installs, inspects, and removes the shell adapter [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]safely and honestly; and `just install` installs bob from source [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and keeps its shell completion current in one step.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bob_shell_completion.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/bob_shell_completion.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-3j[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-3j/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One composed clap command tree for completion[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]one-tree[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]one-tree: build an exhaustive, completion-only clap tree from the module[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]builders plus descriptors for the five hand-parsed commands and the bare[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default-subcommand forms, guarded by parity, parse-smoke, and help-drift[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests, with no user-visible change.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hidden __complete endpoint, protocol 1, and static value kinds[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after one-tree[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine: pin clap_complete's dynamic engine behind one module, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]early-intercepted hidden __complete endpoint speaking protocol 1, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kinds table with static decisions, the presenter rules and groups, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coverage and golden tests, and the first docs/completion.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The bob-owned zsh adapter[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]zsh-adapter[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]zsh-adapter: ship the embedded, protocol-stamped _bob zsh adapter that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renders grouped, described, natively styled menus, completes on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]first autoloaded TAB, and is covered by stubbed-compsys and real-zpty [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob completion command, adapter lifecycle, and just install[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lifecycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after zsh-adapter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lifecycle: add the public bob completion command (status default, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]install, uninstall, zsh) with target discovery, ownership stamp plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]manifest, atomic writes, real-shell verification and beautiful stacked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reports, then the just install recipe, install-smoke checks, README, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Vault-aware value kinds with partial-parse context[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-kinds[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-kinds: add partial-parse context and read-only vault providers for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]routes, sections, tasks, task sections, Pomodoro refs, plugins, levels, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and vault notes, behind a 150 ms deadline, with a read-only enforcement [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test and fixture-vault goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture markers inside capture TEXT[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-text[dim] · [dim][/dim]after vault-kinds[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-text: complete capture markers at the end of the active TEXT [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]word through an in-process capture_complete extraction, honoring the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release gates (boundary, safe rows only, end of word only, no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wikilinks), using the !prefix directive.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bash adapter and bash lifecycle support[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bash[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lifecycle, capture-text[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bash: add the values-only bash adapter with COMP_LINE word reassembly [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and wordbreak-safe replies, wire bash into install/status/uninstall and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verification, and cover it with real-bash tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end polish, performance record, and docs finish[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bash[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]polish: run a sandboxed end-to-end zsh session, record real latency on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the vault, replace illustrative docs samples with real transcripts from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the fixture vault, and sweep help text and output for cli_rules and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual consistency.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-3j","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-3j.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e9a1c3262f63d0a9adbac2ff95b36925","started_at":"2026-10-02T15:06:52.079650+00:00","state":"active"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.1","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.2","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.3","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.4","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.5","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.6","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.7","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.8","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.9","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.9.1","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.9.2","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.9.land","bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-3j.land"]}
